143:3, Rivera v. Crawford, No. 1:25-CV-1793, ECF No. 8 (E.D. Va. Nov. 14, 2025).3 During the subsequent bond hearings, immigration judges concluded that Lopez Garcia and Rivera posed no danger to the community or a risk of flight. In November 2025, both men were released from detention on bond. The Government timely appealed the decisions granting habeas relief and the cases were consolidated on appeal. We possess jurisdiction under 28 U.S.C. §§ 1291 and 2253(a).
