l. There he advances a wholly separate argument: that Petitioner’s claims are not cognizable in habeas. That was not raised by the government and accordingly not addressed by the panel. We write briefly to respond to this novel argument.1 1 We do not address the novel and unrelated contentions raised by Judge Schwartz in his concurrence in the denial of rehearing en banc. It is not the role of judges to advise
